+    // Beyond the device cache, read further down each ranking with ordinary buffered reads so
+    // the slabs end up on the standby list. This is what the demand misses would otherwise
+    // spend hundreds of tokens doing.
+    // Warming is itself an I/O job, so it uses the same per-worker handles as the loader:
+    // on one shared handle this loop ran at ~1 GB/s and a 16 GiB warm was unaffordable.
